  "caveats": [
    "Component count is a NECESSARY condition on the closure, so an empty intersection refutes while a survivor is only a candidate. Cusp count equals component count for link exteriors and the census is not exhausted by link exteriors, so the arity-restricted counts are UPPER bounds on genuine link candidates — the emptiness at 2H/3H only strengthens.",
    "The census-degeneracy measurement (A5) is prior work, docs/audits/2026-08-25-knot-id-is-an-admitted-fit.md; it is re-measured here as a guard, not claimed. The counts differ slightly because that audit counted STRICTLY closer over OrientableCuspedCensus alone and this counts AT LEAST AS GOOD over OCC + HTLinkExteriors.",
